          "statement": "The paper lacks a discussion on the real-world and societal implications of the theoretical bounds, such as how these guarantees might influence the design of fairer or more robust FL systems in sensitive domains like healthcare or finance.",
          "source_roles": [
            "SIGN"
          ],
          "evidence_anchors": [
            "SRC-001"
          ],
          "suggestions": [
            "Add a brief discussion on how these theoretical insights can guide practitioners in ensuring model reliability and fairness for unparticipating clients in practical applications."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "role": "ORIG",
      "opinions": [
        {
          "statement": "The paper introduces a meaningful new problem formulation by explicitly analyzing the generalization error for unparticipating clients in federated learning, a gap largely ignored by previous works that focused only on participating clients.",
          "source_roles": [
            "ORIG"
          ],
          "evidence_anchors": [
            "SRC-002",
            "SRC-004"
          ],
          "suggestions": []
        },
