          "source_roles": [
            "ORIG"
          ],
          "evidence_anchors": [
            "SRC-011",
            "SRC-015"
          ],
          "suggestions": []
        },
        {
          "statement": "The analysis provides novel insights by decomposing the excess risk for unparticipating clients into participating error and participation gap, clarifying how the number of participating clients and local sample size affect generalization in a heterogeneous environment.",
          "source_roles": [
            "ORIG"
          ],
          "evidence_anchors": [
            "SRC-008",
            "SRC-014"
          ],
          "suggestions": []
        },
        {
          "statement": "The paper is purely theoretical and does not propose new experimental setups, benchmarks, or datasets to empirically validate the derived bounds or the impact of the participation gap.",
          "source_roles": [
            "ORIG"
          ],
          "evidence_anchors": [
            "SRC-001"
          ],
          "suggestions": [
            "Consider adding a small-scale empirical study to validate the theoretical rates, particularly for the unparticipating client scenario."
          ]
        },
        {
          "statement": "The combination of the two-level distribution framework with small-ball methods for unbounded losses is a creative and well-justified approach to address the limitations of standard concentration inequalities in heavy-tailed federated settings.",
          "source_roles": [
            "ORIG"
          ],
          "evidence_anchors": [
            "SRC-015",
            "SRC-016"
          ],
          "suggestions": []
        },
        {
          "statement": "The paper provides a critical assessment of existing limitations, such as bounded loss assumptions and expectation-form bounds, and addresses them, rather than focusing on negative results.",
          "source_roles": [
            "ORIG"
          ],
          "evidence_anchors": [
            "SRC-003"
          ],
          "suggestions": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "role": "POL",
      "opinions": [
        {
          "statement": "The paper adheres to double-blind review policies by using \"Anonymous authors\" and explicitly stating \"Paper under double-blind review\" in the header, with no visible institutional affiliations or self-identifying acknowledgments.",
          "source_roles": [
            "POL"
          ],
          "evidence_anchors": [
            "SRC-001"
          ],
          "suggestions": []
        },
