          "statement": "The paper lacks a dedicated \"Broader Impact\" or \"Ethical Considerations\" section, which is typically required by modern conference guidelines, especially for federated learning research involving sensitive data.",
          "source_roles": [
            "POL"
          ],
          "evidence_anchors": [
            "SRC-001",
            "SRC-028"
          ],
          "suggestions": [
            "Add a brief \"Broader Impact\" section discussing the implications of improved generalization bounds for federated learning, particularly regarding privacy-preserving machine learning and the potential for deploying models on diverse, heterogeneous data sources."
          ]
        },
        {
          "statement": "The research is theoretical in nature and does not involve the collection of new data, training of models on sensitive datasets, or direct deployment, thus presenting no immediate ethical risks regarding fairness, bias, or harm to marginalized populations.",
          "source_roles": [
